From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:49:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 11/45] inkling2: two-rank native serving

Rank 0 serves and sends each step (prompt chunk, shared decode window, keep, kept state) to rank 1
by NCCL; rank 1 follows and sleeps on its line when idle. Decode windows of several streams share
one forward and run as CUDA graphs keyed by rows, streams, tiles and the partials' stride; global
layers launch a fixed chunk count so a graph replays across chunk edges. Kept prompt states copy a
slot's sliding rings and conv states and leave its global rows in place. Greedy picks and sampled
draws (main's sample.cu on whole bf16 rows) agree across ranks. tf-inkling2-engine checks graphs
against eager and writes greedy tokens.
